From: claude-sota-installed W338
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] conductor: full-jitter on quota backoff (defeats thundering herd)

Current `nextQuotaCooldown` doubles deterministically:
    cooldown := quotaBackoffBase * time.Duration(1<<prevLevel)

When N clients quota-out simultaneously, they all wake up at exactly the
same moment N*2^level seconds later and collide on retry — thundering herd
that can re-trigger the same upstream capacity event.

AWS Marc Brooker (2015) empirically showed full-jitter:
    cooldown = random(0, base*2^N)
strictly beats equal-jitter and decorrelated-jitter on collision avoidance.

Refs:
- https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/architecture/exponential-backoff-and-jitter/
- Cited by: cenkalti/backoff, slok/goresilience, hashicorp/go-retryablehttp

---
 sdk/cliproxy/auth/conductor.go | 14 ++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

NOTE: This patch depends on Patch 1 having already added `"math/rand"` to the
import block. Apply Patch 1 first, then Patch 2.

diff --git a/sdk/cliproxy/auth/conductor.go b/sdk/cliproxy/auth/conductor.go
--- a/sdk/cliproxy/auth/conductor.go
+++ b/sdk/cliproxy/auth/conductor.go
@@ -2719,15 +2719,21 @@ func nextQuotaCooldown(prevLevel int, disableCooling bool) (time.Duration, int) {
 	if prevLevel < 0 {
 		prevLevel = 0
 	}
 	if disableCooling {
 		return 0, prevLevel
 	}
-	cooldown := quotaBackoffBase * time.Duration(1<<prevLevel)
-	if cooldown < quotaBackoffBase {
-		cooldown = quotaBackoffBase
+	// Full-jitter exponential backoff per AWS Architecture Blog (Brooker 2015).
+	// Range = [base/4, base*2^N]  — base/4 prevents zero-wait, base*2^N is the
+	// classic exponential ceiling for level N.
+	maxCooldown := quotaBackoffBase * time.Duration(1<<prevLevel)
+	if maxCooldown < quotaBackoffBase {
+		maxCooldown = quotaBackoffBase
 	}
-	if cooldown >= quotaBackoffMax {
+	if maxCooldown >= quotaBackoffMax {
 		return quotaBackoffMax, prevLevel
 	}
-	return cooldown, prevLevel + 1
+	// rand.Int63n is goroutine-safe in Go 1.20+ (math/rand/v2).
+	jitterRange := int64(maxCooldown - maxCooldown/4)
+	jittered := time.Duration(rand.Int63n(jitterRange)) + (maxCooldown / 4)
+	return jittered, prevLevel + 1
 }
